# The dynchar parity HARNESS is tracked; the data it chews through is not.
#
# These scripts were lost once and rebuilt from scratch, which cost real work — the reference
# beat map, the trim offsets, the dropout guard and the QA classifier all live here. What must
# NOT be tracked is the capture corpus and the render output, which run to several GB.

# Reference captures and recovery snapshots (~3.4 GB).
opcheck/REF_NEW/
opcheck/REF/
opcheck/RECOVERY/

# Instrumentation and deps, both reproducible.
opcheck/frida/
opcheck/node_modules/

# Rendered frames, clips and their staging dirs.
*.png
*.jpg
*.mp4
parity-clips/fresh8/
parity-clips/f_*/

# Superseded artifact-update iterations — `refresh_artifact.py` is the live one and is tracked.
parity-clips/update_artifact*.py

# Scratch prompts and captured logs.
*.txt
*.log

# Generated by parity-clips/build_page.py (7-8 MB of inlined video).
parity-clips/parity_page.html

# Pulled game data and generated analysis dumps — all reproducible from the client or from a
# probe, and none of it is harness. `skin_table_cur` / `shop_client_table` / `hot_update_list`
# are straight client pulls; `scoreable_skins*` and `l2d_entrance_catalog` are census output
# (which skins have a `DynEntranceId` the Lookbook can actually reach); `fit_chyue` is one
# sweep's fit; `cetnat/` is a capture staging dir.
opcheck/skin_table_cur.json
opcheck/shop_client_table.json
opcheck/hot_update_list.json
opcheck/scoreable_skins.json
opcheck/scoreable_skins.FULL.json
opcheck/l2d_entrance_catalog.json
opcheck/fit_chyue.json
opcheck/cetnat/
